*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# **Raw machine reports are committed exactly as the machine wrote them**, CRLF included — a
# `STARBASE` inspection is evidence, and normalising its bytes would make the committed copy
# something other than the artifact the run produced. Without this, `git diff --check` reports every
# line of one as trailing whitespace, which is a false positive a reviewer has to re-derive each
# time (2026-08-29 review of `ai/evidence/2026-08-29-T268-starbase-orphan-wait-reasons.txt`). No
# `text` attribute is set, so git neither converts nor claims to.
ai/evidence/*.txt whitespace=-trailing-space
